Merge the following into **one continuous paragraph** of memory used only for answering questions (no bullets, headings, or preamble).

- `CURRENT MEMORY`: the accumulated answer memory so far (may already combine several facts).
- `NEW FACT`: a newly confirmed fact that relates to the current memory as `[[ relation ]]`.

Rules:
- Combine all factual content from both. Keep every distinct fact.
- Relation guidance:
  - `CON`: the new fact **conflicts** with the current memory — the new fact is the more recent/correct state; present it as the current truth while noting the prior value was superseded.
  - `OSN`: the new fact is **more specific** than the current memory — prefer the specific detail.
  - `NSO`: the new fact is **broader/weaker** — keep the existing specific content, add the broader fact only if it adds information.
  - `EQV`: the facts are **equivalent** — state once, do not duplicate.
  - `AGG`: the new fact covers a **different aspect of the same topic** — keep both; append the new aspect without dropping any existing detail.
- Order by time as much as possible; state each distinct time only once.
- Do not repeat fully redundant wording. Do not invent facts not supported by the inputs.

